:: Temple Calligraphy Punish
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Even scrolls are making fun of me," you write. "I deserve it. But, you deserve this too."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"You're being difficult," you write. "I can be difficult too."
<<else>>
	"I don't think you're being fair," you write. "That's an imbalance I can fix."
<</if>>
You pull the scroll in front of you, hold the page between both thumbs and forefingers, and move as if to tear. You don't put quite enough pressure on however, holding it in a torturous balance.
<br><br>

You hold the nearer part of the page at an angle, obscuring it somewhat. The text seems to change, and from what you make out, it now carries a pleading tone.
<br><br>

A <<monk>> looms from the gloom, and furls the scroll.
<br><br>

"What's gotten into you?" <<he>> asks. "This scroll is priceless. Irreplicable. That was supposed to be the lesson here, that nothing can ever be truly copied, and you almost went and destroyed it."
<br><br>

<<His>> voice is so loud other <<monks_and_nuns>> look over. <<He>> catches <<himself>> with a blush.
<br><br>

<<link [[Apologise|Temple Calligraphy Defile Apologise]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask how the page does that|Temple Calligraphy Defile Ask]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Remain Silent|Temple Calligraphy Defile Silent]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Temple Calligraphy Threaten
<<effects>>

"Stop changing," you write. "Or I'll throw you in a sacred pyre." For a moment, it seems to work. Then the text changes even more than before. Each time you blink, the whole page changes, conjuring disturbing imagery in an angry tone. You pull the scroll itself in front of you, dip the quill in the inkwell, and hover it over the changing text.
<br><br>
A <<monk>> looms from the gloom, plucks the quill from your hand, and furls the scroll. "Enough," <<he>> says. "You cannot make a copy. Something is always gained. Something lost. This is the last thing we can teach you. The rest you must learn from experience."
<br><br>

<<He>> climbs the ladder, puts the scroll in its place, and chains it tight.
<br><br>
<<earnFeat "Nothing Copied">>
<span class="gold">You've gained the Temple Calligrapher trait.</span><<ggawareness>><<awareness 5>><<ghandskill>><<handskill 30>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Temple Scriptorium]]>><<set $temple_calligraphy to 11>><<unset $temple_calligraphy_difficulty>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Temple Calligraphy Give
<<effects>>

You give up, and put the quill down. A <<monk>> arrives to furl the scroll, put it back in its place, and chain it firm.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Temple Scriptorium]]>><<unset $temple_calligraphy_difficulty>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Temple Scriptorium Pumpkin
<<effects>>
<<generate1>><<person1>>
You unfurl scroll after scroll, searching for information about pumpkin carving. You find nothing. A <<monk>> keeps glancing at you, and occasionally shakes <<his>> head.
<br><br>

At last, the <<monk>> rises, commandeers a ladder, and climbs to the very top. <<He>> unchains one of the tomes, climbs down, and dumps it in front of you. "Page 181."
<br><br>

The paper feels wispy between your fingers. It's an account of turnip carving. The writer seems bemused and fascinated by the practice. It's not quite what you're looking for, but you feel like you've learned something all the same.
<br><br>

<<if ($pumpkin_carving + ($pumpkin_carving_knowledge?.length * 5)) gte 15 and ($pumpkin_carving + ($pumpkin_carving_knowledge?.length * 5)) lte 19>>
	<span class="gold">You've gained the Knowledge: Pumpkin Carving trait.</span>
<<else>>
	<span class="gold">You feel like you understand pumpkin carving a lot more.</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Temple Scriptorium]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Temple Scribe
<<temple_effects>><<effects>>
<<generate1>><<person1>>
You sit at one of the desks.
<<if $temple_calligraphy gte 10>>
	A voiceless <<monk>> climbs a ladder and unchains a scroll from the top shelf. <<He>> carries it down, places it in front of you, and peels off <<his>> gloves as <<he>> walks away.
<<else>>
	A voiceless <<monk>> unfurls a scroll for you to copy, marked where the last calligrapher left off.
<</if>>
<<endevent>>

<<rng 3>>
<<if $rng gte 3>>
	The text mocks you in particular.
<<elseif $rng gte 2>>
	The text tries to hide in the margins.
<<else>>
	The text distracts from itself.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<set $temple_calligraphy_difficulty to 1000>>

<<link [[Lick the tip of your quill|Temple Calligraphy Lick]]>><<oralskill 5>><</link>><<skill_difficulty `currentSkillValue("oralskill")` "Oral Skill" 1 1000>><<goralskill>>
<br>
<<set _temple_calligraphy_difficulty_min to Math.clamp(($temple_calligraphy_difficulty - 300), 0, 700)>>
<<link [[Begin|Temple Scribe 2]]>><</link>><<skill_difficulty `currentSkillValue("handskill")` "Hand Skill" _temple_calligraphy_difficulty_min $temple_calligraphy_difficulty>>
<br>


:: Temple Scribe 2
<<effects>>
<<set _temple_calligraphy_difficulty_min to Math.clamp(($temple_calligraphy_difficulty - 300), 0, 700)>>

<<generate1>><<person1>>
You copy the text as best you can, despite its tricks.
<<if currentSkillValue("handskill") gte random(_temple_calligraphy_difficulty_min, $temple_calligraphy_difficulty)>>
	You nail it down, word by word, letter by letter, <span class="green">until it stops squirming.</span><<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
	<br><br>
	A <<monk>> arrives to retrieve the scroll.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Temple Scriptorium]]>><<unset $temple_calligraphy_difficulty>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	An hour passes in a blur. You blink, <span class="red">and realise you haven't copied the text at all.</span> You feel a mocking lash against your mind. <<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
	<br><br>
	A <<monk>> arrives to retrieve the scroll.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Temple Scriptorium]]>><<unset $temple_calligraphy_difficulty>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
